verses.text:
So the law grows numb,
and justice never goes forth;
for the wicked hem in the righteous;
so justice goes forth twisted.

Its horses are swifter than leopards,
and keener than wolves at evening.
Its horsemen gallop proudly;
its horsemen come from far away;
they fly like an eagle swooping to devour.

They all come for violence;
the set of their faces is forward;{d}
they gather captives like sand.

Are you not eternal,
Yahweh my God, my Holy One?
We will not perish.{f}
Yahweh, you have set them in place to punish us;
Rock, you have established them to correct us.

He lifts them all up with the angle;
he hauls them away in his net
and gathers them in his dragnet;
therefore he rejoices and exults.

Upon my watch I will stand,
and set myself upon the tower;
I will look out to see what he will speak with me,
and what reply I shall make to my complaint.{a}

And Yahweh answered me and said:
“Write the vision;
make it plain upon tablets,
so that one may run who reads it.{b}

For the vision is still for the appointed time;
it hastens toward the end, and it will not lie.
If it seems slow, wait for it;
for it will surely come; it will not delay.{c}

“Behold, the one who is puffed up,
his soul is not upright within him;
but the righteous shall live by his faithfulness.{d}

“Wine, moreover, is a traitor;{e}
the proud man never rests at home.
His appetite gapes wide as Sheol,{f}
and like death he is never full.
He rakes in every nation
and gathers up all peoples.”

You have devised shame for your house
by cutting off many peoples;
you have sinned against your own soul.

Behold, is it not from Yahweh of Armies{g}
that peoples toil only for the fire,
and nations weary themselves for nothing?

For the earth shall be filled
with the knowledge of the glory of Yahweh,
as the waters cover the sea.{h}

Woe to him who makes his neighbors drink,
pouring out your wrath and making them drunk,
in order to look upon their nakedness!{i}

The violence you did to Lebanon will overwhelm you,
and the slaughter of its animals will terrify you,{k}
for human bloodshed and violence to the land,
to cities and everyone who lives in them.

Yahweh, I have heard of your fame,
and I am awestruck.
Yahweh, renew your deeds in our own time;
make them known in these years;
in your anger, remember compassion.{b}

His shining was as the light of day;
rays came forth from his hand,{d}
and there was the hiding of his power.

He stood and measured the earth;{f}
he looked and made the nations tremble.
The everlasting mountains were shattered;
the ancient hills sank low.
His goings are as of old.

Your bow was laid bare;
the arrows were sworn by your word.{h} Selah
You split the earth with rivers.

The mountains saw you and writhed;
the torrent of waters swept by;{i}
the deep uttered its voice
and raised its hands on high.

With his own spears you stabbed the heads of his warriors,{j}
who rushed out like a storm to scatter me,
gloating as though devouring the helpless in hiding.

I heard, and my body trembled;
my lips quivered at the sound;
rottenness entered into my bones;
I trembled where I stood,
because I must wait quietly for the day of distress
to come upon the people who invade us.

Though the fig tree does not blossom,
and no grapes grow on the vines;
though the olive harvest fails,
and the fields yield no grain;
though the sheep vanish from the pen,
and no cattle stand in the barns,

Yahweh, the Lord, is my strength;{k}
he makes my feet like the feet of deer,
and makes me tread upon my high places.
For the choir director: on my stringed instruments.{l}
